1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:06,817
Water, earth,

2
00:00:06,901 --> 00:00:10,195
fire, air...

3
00:00:11,322 --> 00:00:15,367
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

4
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:18,745
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

5
00:00:19,789 --> 00:00:23,709
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

6
00:00:23,793 --> 00:00:25,627
But when the world needed him most,

7
00:00:25,712 --> 00:00:27,004
he vanished.

8
00:00:27,422 --> 00:00:31,216
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

9
00:00:31,301 --> 00:00:32,884
an airbender named Aang.

10
00:00:32,969 --> 00:00:35,262
And although his
airbending skills are great,

11
00:00:35,346 --> 00:00:38,015
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

12
00:00:38,975 --> 00:00:42,269
But I believe Aang can save the world.

13
00:00:59,162 --> 00:01:02,205
The Earth Kingdom City of Omashu!

14
00:01:05,168 --> 00:01:07,210
I used to always come here
to visit my friend Bumi.

15
00:01:07,295 --> 00:01:08,420
Wow!

16
00:01:08,504 --> 00:01:10,672
We don't have cities like this
in the South Pole.

17
00:01:10,882 --> 00:01:13,258
They have buildings here
that don't melt.

18
00:01:13,343 --> 00:01:14,843
Well, let's go, slowpokes.

19
00:01:14,927 --> 00:01:17,763
The real fun is inside the city!

20
00:01:17,847 --> 00:01:19,348
Wait, Aang.

21
00:01:19,432 --> 00:01:20,599
It could be dangerous

22
00:01:20,683 --> 00:01:22,184
if people find out you're the Avatar.

23
00:01:22,268 --> 00:01:23,643
You need a disguise.

24
00:01:23,728 --> 00:01:25,604
So, what am I supposed to do,

25
00:01:25,688 --> 00:01:26,938
grow a mustache?

26
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,777
This is so itchy.

27
00:01:31,861 --> 00:01:34,071
How do you live in this stuff?

28
00:01:35,907 --> 00:01:36,990
Great!

29
00:01:37,075 --> 00:01:38,492
Now you look just like my grandfather.

30
00:01:38,701 --> 00:01:41,036
Technically, Aang is 112 years old.

31
00:01:42,497 --> 00:01:44,873
Now, let's get to skipping,
young whipper snappers!

32
00:01:45,083 --> 00:01:46,333
The big city awaits!

33
00:02:02,767 --> 00:02:04,768
You guys are gonna love Omashu.

34
00:02:04,852 --> 00:02:07,479
The people here are the friendliest
in the world.

35
00:02:09,232 --> 00:02:11,858
What kind of slum
do you think this is?

36
00:02:17,990 --> 00:02:19,866
No! My cabbages!

37
00:02:22,829 --> 00:02:24,538
Just keep smiling.

38
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:27,499
Heh heh heh.

39
00:02:30,878 --> 00:02:32,337
State your business!

40
00:02:33,631 --> 00:02:35,757
My business is my business, young man,

41
00:02:35,842 --> 00:02:37,217
and none of yours.

42
00:02:37,301 --> 00:02:39,177
I've got half a mind
to bend you over my knee

43
00:02:39,262 --> 00:02:40,720
and paddle your backside.

44
00:02:40,805 --> 00:02:42,764
Settle down, old timer.

45
00:02:42,849 --> 00:02:44,224
Just tell me who you are.

46
00:02:44,308 --> 00:02:49,187
Name's Bonzoo Pippenpadlopsicopolis
the Third.

47
00:02:49,272 --> 00:02:51,314
And these are my grandkids.

48
00:02:51,399 --> 00:02:53,525
Hi. June Pippenpadlopsicopolis.

49
00:02:53,609 --> 00:02:54,609
Nice to meet you.

50
00:02:56,279 --> 00:02:58,864
You seem like
a responsible young lady.

51
00:02:58,948 --> 00:03:01,241
See that your grandfather
stays out of trouble.

52
00:03:01,325 --> 00:03:02,325
Enjoy Omashu.

53
00:03:02,410 --> 00:03:03,618
We will.

54
00:03:06,956 --> 00:03:08,123
Wait a minute!

55
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:13,003
You're a strong young boy.

56
00:03:13,087 --> 00:03:14,546
Show some respect for the elderly

57
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:16,548
and carry your grandfather's bag.

58
00:03:17,258 --> 00:03:18,550
Good idea.

59
00:03:46,454 --> 00:03:48,914
This is
the Omashu delivery system...

60
00:03:49,123 --> 00:03:51,374
Miles and miles of tubes and chutes.

61
00:03:53,753 --> 00:03:56,379
Earthbending brings the packages up,

62
00:03:56,464 --> 00:03:58,381
and gravity brings them down.

63
00:03:59,383 --> 00:04:01,384
Great, so they get their mail on time.

64
00:04:01,469 --> 00:04:03,094
They do get their mail on time.

65
00:04:03,179 --> 00:04:06,681
But my friend Bumi
found a better use for these chutes.

66
00:04:10,269 --> 00:04:11,478
Look around you!

67
00:04:11,562 --> 00:04:12,562
What do you see?!

68
00:04:12,647 --> 00:04:15,273
Um... The mail system.

69
00:04:15,358 --> 00:04:17,317
Instead of seeing
what they want you to see,

70
00:04:17,401 --> 00:04:20,403
you gotta open your brain
to the possibilities.

71
00:04:20,488 --> 00:04:22,822
A package-sending system?

72
00:04:22,907 --> 00:04:25,909
The world's greatest super slide!

73
00:04:25,993 --> 00:04:28,703
Bumi, you're a mad genius.

74
00:04:36,003 --> 00:04:37,629
Yeah! Ha ha ha ha!

75
00:04:40,633 --> 00:04:41,800
One ride...

76
00:04:42,051 --> 00:04:43,843
Then we're off to the North Pole...

77
00:04:43,928 --> 00:04:45,220
Airbender's honor.

78
00:04:45,304 --> 00:04:46,429
This sounded like fun at first,

79
00:04:46,514 --> 00:04:48,598
but now that I'm here,

80
00:04:48,683 --> 00:04:52,227
I'm starting to have second thoughts!

81
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,733
Yeah!

82
00:04:58,943 --> 00:05:00,360
Ha ha ha ha!

83
00:05:14,750 --> 00:05:15,834
I'm on it!

84
00:05:20,798 --> 00:05:24,092
Men, you'll be going off
to combat soon.

85
00:05:24,176 --> 00:05:26,845
It's important that you be prepared
for anything.

86
00:05:36,022 --> 00:05:37,564
Aang, do something!

87
00:05:37,648 --> 00:05:39,357
Use your airbending!

88
00:05:39,442 --> 00:05:41,151
Yeah! Good idea!

89
00:05:41,235 --> 00:05:43,028
That will make us go even faster.

90
00:06:18,856 --> 00:06:19,939
Sorry!

91
00:06:37,083 --> 00:06:38,667
My cabbages!

92
00:06:38,751 --> 00:06:40,251
You're gonna pay for this!

93
00:06:42,088 --> 00:06:43,546
Two cabbages, please.

94
00:06:57,978 --> 00:06:59,145
Your Majesty,

95
00:06:59,230 --> 00:07:01,606
these juveniles were arrested
for vandalism,

96
00:07:01,691 --> 00:07:03,066
traveling under false pretenses,

97
00:07:03,150 --> 00:07:04,818
and malicious destruction of cabbages.

98
00:07:04,902 --> 00:07:06,194
Off with their heads!

99
00:07:06,278 --> 00:07:07,987
One for each head of cabbage!

100
00:07:08,072 --> 00:07:09,364
Silence!

101
00:07:09,448 --> 00:07:11,700
Only the king can pass down judgment.

102
00:07:11,784 --> 00:07:13,284
What is your judgment, sire?

103
00:07:25,881 --> 00:07:28,174
Throw them...

104
00:07:28,259 --> 00:07:29,342
A feast.

105
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:42,731
The people in my city

106
00:07:42,815 --> 00:07:45,734
have gotten fat from too many feasts.

107
00:07:45,818 --> 00:07:49,070
So, I hope you like your chicken
with no skin.

108
00:07:49,155 --> 00:07:50,822
Thanks, but I don't eat meat.

109
00:07:50,906 --> 00:07:52,407
How about you?

110
00:07:52,491 --> 00:07:54,409
I bet you like meat.

111
00:07:56,954 --> 00:07:58,163
Is it just me,

112
00:07:58,372 --> 00:08:00,874
or is this guy's crown
a little crooked?

113
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:04,085
So, tell me, young bald one,

114
00:08:04,295 --> 00:08:05,587
where are you from?

115
00:08:06,714 --> 00:08:08,840
I'm from Kangaroo Island.

116
00:08:09,425 --> 00:08:12,010
Kangaroo Island?

117
00:08:12,094 --> 00:08:15,054
I hear that place is really hopping.

118
00:08:21,312 --> 00:08:22,312
What?

119
00:08:22,438 --> 00:08:23,605
It was pretty funny.

120
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:29,360
All these good jokes
are making me tired.

121
00:08:29,445 --> 00:08:31,905
Guess it's time to hit the hay.

122
00:08:36,577 --> 00:08:38,620
There's an airbender in our presence,

123
00:08:38,704 --> 00:08:41,664
and not just any airbender...

124
00:08:41,749 --> 00:08:43,082
The Avatar.

125
00:08:45,503 --> 00:08:47,921
Now, what do you have to
say for yourself,

126
00:08:48,005 --> 00:08:50,298
Mr. Pippenpadlopsicopolis?

127
00:08:56,972 --> 00:08:59,140
Ok, you caught me.

128
00:08:59,225 --> 00:09:00,809
I'm the Avatar...

129
00:09:00,893 --> 00:09:02,393
Doing my Avatar thing,

130
00:09:02,603 --> 00:09:04,145
keeping the world safe.

131
00:09:04,230 --> 00:09:05,647
Everything checks out.

132
00:09:05,731 --> 00:09:07,273
No firebenders here.

133
00:09:07,358 --> 00:09:08,775
So, good work, everybody.

134
00:09:08,859 --> 00:09:09,859
Love each other,

135
00:09:09,944 --> 00:09:10,944
respect all life,

136
00:09:11,111 --> 00:09:12,946
and don't run with your spears.

137
00:09:13,030 --> 00:09:14,322
We'll see you next time!

138
00:09:17,451 --> 00:09:18,868
You can't keep us here.

139
00:09:18,953 --> 00:09:20,286
Let us leave!

140
00:09:21,413 --> 00:09:22,622
Lettuce leaf?

141
00:09:25,709 --> 00:09:27,210
We're in serious trouble.

142
00:09:27,419 --> 00:09:28,962
This guy is nuts.

143
00:09:29,338 --> 00:09:33,424
Tomorrow, the Avatar will face
three deadly challenges.

144
00:09:33,884 --> 00:09:37,303
But for now, the guards
will show you to your chamber.

145
00:09:37,388 --> 00:09:40,181
My liege, do you mean
the good chamber or the bad chamber?

146
00:09:40,266 --> 00:09:41,975
The newly-refurbished chamber.

147
00:09:42,184 --> 00:09:44,352
Wait. Which one are we talking about?

148
00:09:44,562 --> 00:09:47,146
The one that used to be
the bad chamber...

149
00:09:47,231 --> 00:09:49,816
Until the recent refurbishing,
that is.

150
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:52,026
Of course, we've been calling it
the new chamber,

151
00:09:52,111 --> 00:09:53,194
but we really should
number them.

152
00:09:54,488 --> 00:09:56,531
Take them to the refurbished chamber

153
00:09:56,615 --> 00:09:58,283
that was once bad.

154
00:10:07,126 --> 00:10:08,668
This is a prison cell?

155
00:10:08,752 --> 00:10:09,919
But it's so nice.

156
00:10:10,004 --> 00:10:12,213
He did say it was newly refurbished.

157
00:10:12,298 --> 00:10:14,340
Nice or not, we're prisoners.

158
00:10:14,592 --> 00:10:16,843
I wonder what these challenges
are gonna be.

159
00:10:16,927 --> 00:10:19,012
We're not sticking around to find out.

160
00:10:19,096 --> 00:10:20,889
There's gotta be some way out of here.

161
00:10:20,973 --> 00:10:22,098
The air vents!

162
00:10:24,310 --> 00:10:26,019
If you think we're gonna
fit through there,

163
00:10:26,103 --> 00:10:27,645
you're crazier than that king.

164
00:10:27,730 --> 00:10:28,938
We can't.

165
00:10:29,023 --> 00:10:30,481
But Momo can.

166
00:10:32,985 --> 00:10:34,819
Momo, I need you to find Appa

167
00:10:34,904 --> 00:10:36,237
and bust us out of here.

168
00:10:44,246 --> 00:10:45,413
Go on, boy!

169
00:10:45,497 --> 00:10:46,956
Get Appa!

170
00:10:47,708 --> 00:10:50,043
How was Appa supposed to
save us anyway?

171
00:10:50,377 --> 00:10:52,795
Appa is a 10-ton flying bison.

172
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:54,923
I think he could figure something out.

173
00:10:55,633 --> 00:10:58,343
Well, no point arguing about it now.

174
00:10:58,427 --> 00:11:00,219
Get some rest, Aang.

175
00:11:00,304 --> 00:11:02,013
Looks like you'll need it
for tomorrow.

176
00:11:10,814 --> 00:11:12,649
Sokka? Katara?

177
00:11:13,192 --> 00:11:14,484
Where are my friends?

178
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:17,070
The king will free them
if you complete your challenges.

179
00:11:17,279 --> 00:11:18,947
And if I fail?

180
00:11:19,031 --> 00:11:20,156
He didn't say.

181
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,240
Your staff, please?

182
00:11:27,873 --> 00:11:29,791
First, Avatar,

183
00:11:29,875 --> 00:11:31,918
what do you think of my new outfit?

184
00:11:32,002 --> 00:11:33,461
I want your honest opinion.

185
00:11:36,632 --> 00:11:38,424
I'm waiting.

186
00:11:38,550 --> 00:11:39,592
I...

187
00:11:39,677 --> 00:11:40,927
Guess it's fine.

188
00:11:41,011 --> 00:11:42,178
Excellent.

189
00:11:42,262 --> 00:11:43,888
You've passed the first test.

190
00:11:43,973 --> 00:11:44,973
Really?

191
00:11:45,057 --> 00:11:46,099
Well...

192
00:11:46,183 --> 00:11:47,850
Not one of the deadly tests.

193
00:11:47,935 --> 00:11:49,560
The real challenges are much more...

194
00:11:49,645 --> 00:11:50,645
Challenging.

195
00:11:53,941 --> 00:11:56,109
I don't have time
for your crazy games.

196
00:11:56,443 --> 00:11:58,277
Give me my friends back.
We're leaving!

197
00:11:58,737 --> 00:12:01,447
I thought you might refuse,

198
00:12:01,907 --> 00:12:05,785
so I will give your friends
some special souvenirs.

199
00:12:06,161 --> 00:12:07,662
Those delightful rings

200
00:12:07,746 --> 00:12:09,414
are made of pure genomite...

201
00:12:09,790 --> 00:12:12,583
Also known as Creeping Crystal.

202
00:12:12,835 --> 00:12:15,837
It's crystal that grows
remarkably fast.

203
00:12:15,921 --> 00:12:19,590
By nightfall, your friends will be
completely covered in it.

204
00:12:19,675 --> 00:12:21,092
Terrible fate, really.

205
00:12:21,176 --> 00:12:22,552
I can stop it,

206
00:12:22,636 --> 00:12:24,929
but only if you cooperate.

207
00:12:25,973 --> 00:12:27,598
Agh! It's already creeping!

208
00:12:29,184 --> 00:12:30,685
I'll do what you want.

209
00:12:36,150 --> 00:12:38,276
Ha ha ha ha ha!

210
00:12:42,489 --> 00:12:45,074
It seems I've lost my lunchbox key,

211
00:12:45,159 --> 00:12:46,576
and I'm hungry.

212
00:12:50,330 --> 00:12:52,540
There it is!

213
00:12:52,624 --> 00:12:54,208
Would you mind fetching it for me?

214
00:13:11,810 --> 00:13:12,935
Ooh!

215
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:14,312
Climbing the ladder.

216
00:13:14,396 --> 00:13:16,272
No one's thought of that before!

217
00:13:18,901 --> 00:13:19,901
Aah!

218
00:13:45,010 --> 00:13:46,302
That's right.

219
00:13:46,386 --> 00:13:47,762
Keep diving head in.

220
00:13:47,846 --> 00:13:49,597
I'm sure it will work eventually.

221
00:14:05,322 --> 00:14:07,073
There! Enjoy your lunch!

222
00:14:07,282 --> 00:14:09,158
I want my friends back now!

223
00:14:09,326 --> 00:14:10,743
Not yet.

224
00:14:10,828 --> 00:14:12,954
I need help with another matter.

225
00:14:13,038 --> 00:14:16,207
It seems I've lost my pet Flopsy.

226
00:14:17,751 --> 00:14:18,918
Ok, found him.

227
00:14:19,002 --> 00:14:20,044
Bring him to me.

228
00:14:20,379 --> 00:14:22,713
Daddy wants a kiss from Flopsy.

229
00:14:22,881 --> 00:14:24,298
Come here, Flopsy.

230
00:14:25,968 --> 00:14:27,301
Heh heh.

231
00:14:32,349 --> 00:14:33,724
Flopsy, wait!

232
00:14:33,809 --> 00:14:34,976
Flopsy!

233
00:14:38,856 --> 00:14:40,022
Flopsy!

234
00:14:51,285 --> 00:14:52,743
Wait a minute.

235
00:14:56,415 --> 00:14:57,415
Flopsy?

236
00:15:03,255 --> 00:15:04,422
Flopsy!

237
00:15:11,722 --> 00:15:14,015
That's a good boy.

238
00:15:14,099 --> 00:15:16,434
Yes! Who has a soft belly?

239
00:15:19,062 --> 00:15:20,396
Guys, are you ok?

240
00:15:20,689 --> 00:15:23,191
Other than the crystal slowly
encasing my entire body,

241
00:15:23,275 --> 00:15:24,442
doing great.

242
00:15:28,864 --> 00:15:30,489
Yes.

243
00:15:30,866 --> 00:15:33,743
Come on. I'm ready
for the next challenge.

244
00:15:33,827 --> 00:15:36,329
Ha ha ha ha ha!

245
00:15:39,416 --> 00:15:42,084
Your final test is a duel.

246
00:15:42,169 --> 00:15:44,295
And, as a special treat,

247
00:15:44,379 --> 00:15:46,422
you may choose your opponent.

248
00:15:55,432 --> 00:15:56,599
Point and choose.

249
00:15:57,392 --> 00:16:00,436
So, you're saying
whoever I point to...

250
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:02,021
That's the person I get to fight?

251
00:16:03,190 --> 00:16:04,774
Choose wisely.

252
00:16:06,693 --> 00:16:07,985
I...

253
00:16:08,737 --> 00:16:10,238
Choose...

254
00:16:10,322 --> 00:16:11,447
You.

255
00:16:11,531 --> 00:16:13,991
Ha ha. Wrong choice.

256
00:16:24,211 --> 00:16:25,628
Whoa!

257
00:16:26,922 --> 00:16:28,005
Oof!

258
00:16:40,852 --> 00:16:43,646
You thought I was a frail old man,

259
00:16:43,730 --> 00:16:47,441
but I'm the most powerful earthbender
you'll ever see.

260
00:16:47,526 --> 00:16:50,111
Can I fight the guy
with the ax instead?

261
00:16:50,195 --> 00:16:53,990
There are no take-backsies
in my kingdom.

262
00:16:54,074 --> 00:16:55,700
You might need this.

263
00:17:02,249 --> 00:17:04,417
Typical airbender tactic...

264
00:17:04,501 --> 00:17:06,210
Avoid and evade.

265
00:17:06,295 --> 00:17:09,005
I'd hoped the Avatar
would be less predictable.

266
00:17:11,591 --> 00:17:13,801
Don't you have any surprises for me?

267
00:17:13,885 --> 00:17:16,971
Sooner or later,
you'll have to strike back.

268
00:17:32,404 --> 00:17:35,448
You'll have to be
a little more creative than that.

269
00:17:46,335 --> 00:17:49,211
Did someone leave the windows open?

270
00:17:49,296 --> 00:17:51,797
It feels a little drafty in here.

271
00:17:51,882 --> 00:17:54,550
Are you hoping I'll catch a cold?

272
00:18:08,732 --> 00:18:12,234
How are you going to get me
from way over there?

273
00:18:34,049 --> 00:18:35,049
Oof!

274
00:19:19,136 --> 00:19:20,386
Aah!

275
00:19:28,478 --> 00:19:31,355
Ha ha. Well done, Avatar.

276
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:34,567
You fight with much fire
in your heart.

277
00:19:46,371 --> 00:19:49,123
You've passed all my tests.

278
00:19:49,207 --> 00:19:52,251
Now, you must answer one question.

279
00:19:52,335 --> 00:19:53,627
That's not fair.

280
00:19:53,712 --> 00:19:56,255
You said you would release my friends
if I finish your tests.

281
00:19:56,339 --> 00:20:00,134
But what's the point of tests
if you don't learn anything?

282
00:20:00,218 --> 00:20:01,844
Come on!

283
00:20:01,928 --> 00:20:03,888
Answer this one question

284
00:20:03,972 --> 00:20:06,932
and I will set your friends free.

285
00:20:07,017 --> 00:20:09,810
What is my name?

286
00:20:11,021 --> 00:20:12,646
From the looks of your friends,

287
00:20:12,731 --> 00:20:15,357
I'd say you only have a few minutes.

288
00:20:16,276 --> 00:20:17,902
How am I supposed to know his name?

289
00:20:18,195 --> 00:20:19,612
Think about the challenges.

290
00:20:19,696 --> 00:20:21,155
Maybe it's some kind of riddle.

291
00:20:21,239 --> 00:20:22,239
-I got it!
-Yeah?

292
00:20:22,324 --> 00:20:24,116
He's an earthbender, right?

293
00:20:24,201 --> 00:20:25,284
Rocky...

294
00:20:26,703 --> 00:20:28,245
You know, because of all the rocks.

295
00:20:28,413 --> 00:20:29,455
We're gonna keep trying,

296
00:20:29,539 --> 00:20:30,706
but that is a good backup.

297
00:20:30,916 --> 00:20:33,125
Ok, so back to the challenges.

298
00:20:33,210 --> 00:20:35,085
I got a key from a waterfall,

299
00:20:35,170 --> 00:20:37,588
I saved his pet, and I had a duel.

300
00:20:37,714 --> 00:20:38,714
And what did you learn?

301
00:20:39,007 --> 00:20:42,426
Well, everything was different
than I expected.

302
00:20:42,844 --> 00:20:44,553
And...

303
00:20:44,930 --> 00:20:46,055
Well...

304
00:20:46,139 --> 00:20:49,099
They weren't straightforward.
To solve each test,

305
00:20:49,184 --> 00:20:52,561
I had to think differently
than I usually would.

306
00:20:52,646 --> 00:20:54,146
I know his name.

307
00:20:56,316 --> 00:20:59,985
I solved the question
the same way I solved the challenges.

308
00:21:00,070 --> 00:21:02,154
As you said a long time ago,

309
00:21:02,239 --> 00:21:04,990
I had to open my brain
to the possibilities.

310
00:21:08,245 --> 00:21:10,788
Bumi, you're a mad genius.

311
00:21:12,707 --> 00:21:15,668
Aang, it's good to see you.

312
00:21:15,752 --> 00:21:18,462
You haven't changed a bit...

313
00:21:18,547 --> 00:21:19,630
Literally.

314
00:21:20,382 --> 00:21:21,674
Over here.

315
00:21:21,758 --> 00:21:22,758
A little help.

316
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:28,681
Genomite is made of rock candy.

317
00:21:29,849 --> 00:21:30,849
Delicious!

318
00:21:31,226 --> 00:21:34,812
So, this crazy king
is your old friend Bumi?

319
00:21:34,896 --> 00:21:36,313
Who you calling old?

320
00:21:36,982 --> 00:21:38,607
Ok, I'm old.

321
00:21:38,817 --> 00:21:40,276
Why did you do all this

322
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:42,444
instead of just telling Aang
who you were?

323
00:21:42,612 --> 00:21:43,654
First of all,

324
00:21:43,738 --> 00:21:45,656
it's pretty fun messing with people.

325
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:46,824
Ha ha.

326
00:21:46,908 --> 00:21:48,325
But I do have a reason.

327
00:21:48,702 --> 00:21:51,662
Aang, you have a difficult task ahead.

328
00:21:51,746 --> 00:21:54,957
The world has changed in the 100 years
you've been gone.

329
00:21:55,041 --> 00:21:58,252
It's the duty of the Avatar
to restore balance to the world

330
00:21:58,336 --> 00:22:00,754
by defeating Fire Lord Ozai.

331
00:22:00,839 --> 00:22:01,964
You have much to learn.

332
00:22:02,257 --> 00:22:04,341
You must master the four elements

333
00:22:04,426 --> 00:22:06,093
and confront the Fire Lord.

334
00:22:06,177 --> 00:22:07,636
And when you do,

335
00:22:07,721 --> 00:22:10,306
I hope you will think
like a mad genius.

336
00:22:13,935 --> 00:22:16,979
And it looks like
you're in good hands.

337
00:22:17,063 --> 00:22:20,524
You'll need your friends
to help you defeat the Fire Nation.

338
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:24,403
And you'll need Momo, too.

339
00:22:24,654 --> 00:22:26,196
Thank you for your wisdom.

340
00:22:26,281 --> 00:22:27,906
But before we leave,

341
00:22:27,991 --> 00:22:29,867
I have a challenge for you.

342
00:22:31,911 --> 00:22:33,454
-Yeah!
-Whoo!

343
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:39,043
My cabbages!
